# Schoolgirl — the fifth .blob character authored from scratch, and the first
# HUMAN one built to a rigged mesh reference
# (docs/dev-notes/refs/schoolgirl-mesh/schoolgirl.glb, committed 2026-08-23).
# gltfTriangles reads the bind pose, which for this mesh is the clean
# symmetric T-POSE: 1.70 m tall, feet at y=0, facing +z. The mesh holds its
# arms straight out; this .blob rests them down (arms slightly out, ~13 deg,
# to clear the skirt), so blob:measure prints POSE MISMATCH on the whole
# figure and the arm bands are NOT chased — see the range note below.
#
# MEASURED LANDMARKS (from the mesh, 2026-08-22; y and extents as fractions
# of height, x1.70 for metres). Widths are the full silhouette width, so a
# prim's half-width is width/2:
#   crown (fringe peak) 1.000  w .016 d .015
#   skull widest (bob)  .94-.95  w .114 d .134
#   ears (pointed)      .86-.88  w .100 d .123
#   chin / jaw          .855   w .048 d .096
#   neck narrowest      .84    w .048 d .064
#   shoulder            .82    w .217 d .061
#   chest / bust        .72-.74  w .156-.200 d .170
#   waist / belt        .62-.64  w .132 d .106
#   hip / skirt widest  .46-.47  w .239 d .183
#   skirt hem, legs split .455  w .181 d .090
#   knee                .28    w .148 d .059
#   sock top (slouch)   .19-.20  w .164-.172  bulges at the top
#   ankle / shoe top    .07    w .176 d .093
#   sole                .00    w .172 d .170
#
# STYLE: Ichiro Tanida early-2000s Japanese CG — smooth rounded forms, clean
# simple masses, toy-like proportions (6.9 heads tall: mildly stylised, NOT
# chibi). No mottle, no surface noise, hair as a few large smooth masses.
# The outfit is PAINT on the sculpt (color= on prims), exactly as in the
# mesh's texture: skin dab18a, navy 01046d, white ececed, sock d9d8d9,
# hair/shoes 201109, sole bdb9bc, accents 66537c.
model schoolgirl
  height 1.70
  # Checked, not decorative — see blob-checks.ts.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # ROOT: head at the crotch = skirt hem line (0.455 -> 0.7735, where the
  # legs split the silhouette), tail at the hip line 0.820. The mesh's hip
  # sockets sit just under the skirt's widest band (0.46-0.47).
  root pelvis at 0.773 len=0.047

  # Spine: pelvis tail (0.820) up to the waist/belt (0.62 -> 1.054).
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=1 len=0.234
  # Belt to shoulder line (0.82 -> 1.394).
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=1 len=0.340
  # Shoulder up through the neck; the visible neck is 1.428-1.50, the rest
  # runs up inside the head (the house pattern — see mouse.blob).
  bone neck   parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0 len=0.111
  # Positions the face block: facePrims ride skull at=0.45, so this head
  # (1.505) + 0.45*0.155 centres the cranium at 1.575 — midway between the
  # chin (1.4535) and the crown (1.70), where the mesh's skin skull sits
  # under the bob. Authors to the mesh SURFACE, not the rig joints.
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=0 len=0.155

  mirror
    # ARMS REST DOWN, eased IN at the shoulder and swung FORWARD below the
    # elbow so the hands hang clear of the flared skirt. v2's chain
    # 12/-2/-2 (out at the shoulder, easing in below) dropped the hand to
    # (0.144, 0.81, 0.06) — inside the skirt cone, whose sheared end cap
    # holds x 0.19 / z 0.15 at hand height: clearOf(arm, torso) measured
    # -0.011 and the owner saw the lower arms clip INTO the skirt
    # (2026-08-23). The outward route failed the floor: swinging the
    # forearm OUT to clear the cap put arm mass outside the skirt's front
    # outline at the hem band and cost the legs window 0.03 IoU (0.824 ->
    # 0.792, floor 0.80). This chain (tilt 8/4/2, pitch 2/18/12) takes the
    # brief's other escape instead: hands a little IN FRONT of the hem —
    # hand centre (0.153, 0.82, 0.14), in front of z 0.09, while every arm
    # band stays inside the skirt's x outline from the front, so the legs
    # window holds 0.814. Hands stay behind the skirt's front face
    # (z 0.146): resting ON the skirt front, not through it.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    side=0.048 dir=side  len=0.045
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=8 pitch=2 len=0.295
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=4 pitch=18 len=0.260
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=2 pitch=12 len=0.085
    # LEGS: the mesh stance is knees TOGETHER (its knee band is 0.245 wide
    # = 2 x (0.069 centre + 0.0535 radius), inner edges touching) with the
    # calves and socks spreading below — a shy, toes-out schoolgirl stand.
    # Straight vertical columns at x +/-0.069 carry the whole leg.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis   dir=down tilt=0  side=0.069 len=0.344
    bone shin     parent=thigh    dir=down tilt=0          len=0.357
    # The foot bone only positions shoe prims; they are authored as plain
    # world displacements off it (see mouse.blob's shoes).
    bone foot     parent=shin     dir=fwd                  len=0.090
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO (v2, 2026-08-23 — the SMOOTH rebuild). v1 matched every band
  # width and still read as a STACK OF HORIZONTAL DISCS (owner: "straight
  # horrifying") because it was authored as six flat rings. This version is
  # the Tanida construction from the brief: a few large tapered masses on
  # the spine bones, the outfit carried by PAINT (color=) alone — paint
  # changes colour, not shape, so the white top and the skin midriff are
  # the SAME smooth column. NOTE on blend: this lab's smin is kk=4k with a
  # max dip of k (validate.ts), so the brief's "start at 0.05" reaches 20 cm
  # past a prim's own surface — at k 0.045-0.05 the shoulder bar's blend
  # window touched the CROWN (dip 6 mm, broke the 1.70 m height pin) and
  # filled the under-chin hollow. 0.025 (kk 0.10) hides the seams without
  # webbing the neck; the bars overlap 30-50% lengthwise so the surfaces
  # already continue each other. Radii pre-shrunk ~0.01 against inflation. Mesh width/depth halves: bust 0.170/0.144 at
  # 1.224, waist 0.066/0.053 at 1.054, shoulder 0.108/0.030 at 1.394 (thin
  # front-to-back: the collar drapes flat over it).
  # ============================================================
  # Pelvis filler under the skirt (never seen; keeps the legs fused).
  blob torso on pelvis  at=0.50 r=0.090 deep=0.95 blend=0.020 color=dab18a
  # Pelvis-to-waist: one tapered bar, mostly hidden under the skirt; its top
  # is the bottom half of the skin midriff. r 0.072 -> 0.054: the waist's
  # 0.066 half-width minus the k/4 blend inflation.
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.20 to=1.00 r=0.072 r2=0.054 deep=0.88 blend=0.025 color=dab18a
  # The skin midriff band (the top is a CROP TOP; skin shows 1.054-1.105,
  # mesh paint bands 0.62-0.65). Same column as the waist bar, one blend up.
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.00 to=0.16 r=0.054 r2=0.060 deep=0.85 blend=0.025 color=dab18a
  # The WHITE TOP: one tapered bar from the midriff overlap to the bust.
  # The paint boundary with the midriff bar lands at ~1.09-1.11 where the
  # two fields cross — that line is the crop top's hem, and it is a colour
  # change on a smooth surface, not a ledge.
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.10 to=0.62 r=0.060 r2=0.100 deep=1.32 blend=0.025 color=ececed
  # Chest-to-shoulders: the bust up to the shoulder line 0.217 wide but only
  # 0.061 DEEP at 1.394 — deep 0.50 keeps the shoulder band thin
  # front-to-back. It ends LOW (to=0.85, cap top ~1.42) with a tight blend:
  # anything fatter/higher here smin-bridges to the clavicle balls and webs
  # the neck-only band at y 1.445 shut (mesh: 0.073 wide there) — that web
  # alone cost the head window 0.03 IoU until the bar was cut back.
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.58 to=0.85 r=0.074 r2=0.075 deep=0.50 blend=0.012 color=ececed

  # ============================================================
  # THE SKIRT (v2) — ONE flared cone, belt to hem. v1 carried the mesh's
  # hem cliff with two flat ellipsoid RINGS plus six pleat-fragment bars
  # stuck on the thighs; every band measured right and it still read as a
  # CYLINDER WITH A DISC AT THE HEM. The flare is the skirt's whole
  # character (belt half 0.112 at 1.054 -> widest 0.203 at 0.78-0.80), so
  # one cone carries it and the hem is allowed to round under smoothly —
  # the cliff (0.406 -> 0.308 across 2 cm) is a hard-edge read no smooth
  # mass can do, traded away on purpose for the one-piece silhouette.
  # tall 0.42 squashes BOTH end caps along the axis: the bottom cap rounds
  # under in ~0.42*r2 (8 cm) instead of a full r2 ball below the hem (the
  # v1 fat-cap lesson), and the top cap only bulges 4 cm above the belt,
  # so it does not paint the skin midriff navy. NOTE the cap SHEARS: its
  # x/z reach stays near-full down the whole squash, so the bulge's width
  # is r2*wide (0.194 half) wherever it hangs — that is what holds the
  # 0.32+ width at y 0.73 where the mesh's pleat fringe runs, and why r2
  # 0.18 measures worse than 0.185 (the widest ring at 0.79 loses more
  # than the hem band gains). wide 1.05 / deep 0.80: the mesh skirt is
  # wider than deep (0.406 x 0.311 at the widest ring).
  # ============================================================
  blob torso on spine1  at=0.94 r=0.095 r2=0.185 tip=(0,-0.250,0) wide=1.05 tall=0.42 deep=0.80 blend=0.018 color=01046d
  # PLEATS — four shallow grooves riding the cone's slope (front pair and
  # back pair, mirrored), NOT bars standing proud of it. Each groove's axis
  # follows the surface from (y 1.00) to (y 0.82) at the cone's own flare,
  # cutting a 4 mm channel: a pleat LINE, not geometry.
  groove torso on spine1 at=0.77 offset=(0.077,0,0.065) tip=(0.037,-0.180,0.031) r=0.012 depth=0.004 width=0.006 both
  groove torso on spine1 at=0.77 offset=(0.077,0,-0.065) tip=(0.037,-0.180,-0.031) r=0.012 depth=0.004 width=0.006 both

  # ============================================================
  # SAILOR COLLAR (v2) — ONE thin flat prim lying ON the upper chest and
  # back, not a plate around the neck and not v1's cape+yoke stack. Wide
  # across the shoulders, thin vertically, shallow front-to-back; navy.
  # The scarf stays: the small anchor the eye finds first from the front.
  # ============================================================
  blob torso on chest   at=0.92 offset=(0,0.005,-0.010) r=0.070 wide=2.10 tall=0.22 deep=0.70 blend=0.010 color=01046d
  # The scarf, at the chest front centre (y ~1.28), proud of the white top.
  blob torso on chest   at=0.66 offset=(0,-0.010,0.096) r=0.030 wide=1.35 tall=1.05 deep=0.60 blend=0.0040 color=01046d

  # Neck: 0.041 half-wide x 0.054 half-deep (mesh 0.048/0.064 full) at the
  # narrowest 1.428. Skin.
  bar head on neck from=0.18 to=0.78 r=0.041 deep=1.33 blend=0.0040 color=dab18a

  # ============================================================
  # THE HAIR — a swept dark bob with a peaked fringe. Smooth masses, no
  # strands (Tanida: large clean forms). Measured profile (front): the bob
  # runs 0.146 wide at 1.658, 0.17 at 1.642, 0.195-0.219 through 1.56-1.61,
  # 0.196 still at 1.51, then cuts to the ear band 0.146 at 1.476 — a BELL,
  # widest below the crown. One ellipsoid cannot do that, so: a crown shell
  # (the dome) + two side lobes (the flare) + the fringe + the nape + the
  # peak tuft.
  # Crown shell: centre (0,1.612,-0.008), half (0.098, 0.082, 0.113) —
  # 0.195 wide at 1.61, matching the upper run.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,0.037,-0.008) r=0.098 wide=1.00 tall=0.837 deep=1.15 blend=0.0060 color=201109 gloss=0.35
  # The side lobes: the swept flare. Centre (+/-0.074, 1.545, -0.010),
  # half (0.034, 0.045, 0.102) — outer edge 0.108 at 1.545 (0.215 wide,
  # mesh 0.219), bottom edge 1.50, deep in z like the shell.
  # deep 2.2 centred at z -0.030 (was 3.0 at -0.010): the lobes wrapped to
  # z +0.09 and swallowed the cheeks — the mesh's cheeks are open skin with
  # the bob only FRAMING them from behind the ear line.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.074,-0.030,-0.030) r=0.034 wide=1.00 tall=1.32 deep=2.20 blend=0.0060 both color=201109 gloss=0.35
  # The crown peak: the mesh's topmost point is a narrow fringe tip (w .016
  # fraction at y 1.000), not a dome — one tapered bar to a point, tipped
  # slightly forward.
  bar  head on skull from=0.95 to=1.12 offset=(0,0.003,0.012) tip=(0,0.002,0.010) r=0.026 r2=0.007 blend=0.0040 chamfer color=201109 gloss=0.35
  # The fringe: a top-of-forehead RIM, not a brow-covering sweep. The DECAL
  # paints the hairline and the widow's peak itself (the mesh's forehead is
  # OPEN to ~1.56, the peak is 2D art), so geometry that hangs to 1.537
  # covered the whole forehead and the decal then drew a second hairline on
  # the sliver left — a double-hair squeezed wedge (owner, 2026-08-23).
  # Raised ~2 cm and pulled back so the painted forehead shows.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,0.034,0.034) r=0.052 wide=1.30 tall=0.42 deep=0.62 blend=0.0035 color=201109 gloss=0.35
  # The nape: the bob's underside at the back, closing the gap between the
  # lobes' bottom (1.50) and the hairline at the neck. Deep: the mesh side
  # profile at 1.44-1.48 is 0.175-0.207, so the back mass reaches z -0.112
  # and down to y 1.455.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,-0.075,-0.066) r=0.052 wide=0.80 tall=1.10 deep=1.00 blend=0.0050 color=201109 gloss=0.35
  # THE CHIN: the mesh's chin tip sits at (1.45, z 0.095) — 0.10 forward,
  # a definite point on an otherwise small face. One small prim, blended
  # softly into the jaw so it reads as the jaw's tip, not a bead.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,-0.118,0.078) r=0.022 wide=1.20 tall=0.55 deep=0.90 blend=0.0040 color=dab18a

  # EARS — pointed, elf-ish, skin: the mesh's ear band (0.86-0.88 -> y
  # 1.462-1.496) is 0.146-0.170 wide total where the head under the hair is
  # ~0.10, so each ear reaches ~0.076 from the centreline. One tapered prim
  # per side at the hairline's bottom edge, pointing out and slightly back.
  # Bigger and further out than v2 (r 0.012 -> 0.016, x 0.044 -> 0.050):
  # the mesh's ears are a visible feature with earrings, not hidden points.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0.050,-0.097,-0.008) tip=(0.034,0.014,-0.012) r=0.016 r2=0.004 blend=0.0020 chamfer both color=dab18a

  # ============================================================
  # THE FACE — a DECAL (see the sheet block): the mesh's own face, baked
  # flat off schoolgirl.glb and pasted onto the skin cranium the way a PSX
  # face is painted on. v2 had two eye prims and a mouth prim in the accent
  # purple here; they read as a navy visor band (owner, 2026-08-23), and a
  # painted prim replaces albedo AFTER the sheet, so they would sit on top
  # of the decal's eyes. Gone. The skin is left bare for the sheet.
  # ============================================================

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — slim, smooth, rubber-hose simple (no ball joints: Tanida limbs
  # melt). Sleeve WHITE to mid-upper-arm, skin below (mesh: "sleeves short,
  # skin from mid-upper-arm"). The shoulder ball is the arm's core against
  # the torso (house pattern from mouse.blob).
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.048 blend=0.0045 mirror core color=ececed
  # Short sleeve, slightly puffed over the 0.026 arm inside it.
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.00 to=0.45 r=0.034 r2=0.028 blend=0.0050 mirror color=ececed
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.45 to=0.98 r=0.026 r2=0.023 blend=0.0042 mirror color=dab18a
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.00 r=0.023 blend=0.0042 mirror color=dab18a
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.022 r2=0.019 blend=0.0040 mirror color=dab18a
  # Hand: a slim smooth mitt, no fingers — resting hands read as soft
  # masses. The bone's pitch=12 already carries the mitt in front of the
  # hem; offset z 0.03 keeps it just behind the skirt's front face.
  blob arm on hand at=0.45 offset=(0,0,0.03) r=0.028 wide=0.85 tall=1.15 deep=1.25 blend=0.0040 mirror color=dab18a

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — the paint bands do the reading: skin thigh (0.455-0.28 of
  # height: hem to knee), bare knee, then the WHITE SLOUCH SOCK bulging at
  # its top (mesh 0.19-0.20, w .164-.172: 0.0735 half-radius at the cuff,
  # falling to 0.054 at the ankle), then dark shoes.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.00 r=0.062 blend=0.0050 mirror core color=dab18a
  # r 0.0655 -> 0.0535: the mesh column 0.269-0.293 at the thigh tapering
  # to the 0.245 knee band (2 x (0.069 + 0.0535), knees TOUCHING).
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.06 to=0.94 r=0.0655 r2=0.0535 deep=0.85 blend=0.0046 mirror color=dab18a
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 r=0.052 deep=0.85 blend=0.0048 mirror color=dab18a
  # Calf: swells BELOW the knee (mesh 0.269 at 0.375-0.44) toward the cuff.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.10 to=0.38 r=0.060 r2=0.065 deep=0.80 blend=0.0044 mirror color=dab18a
  # The sock: WHITE. The mesh's slouch bunches LOW: 0.292 total at the cuff
  # swelling to 0.304 by 0.147 as the fabric slouches toward the shoe.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.38 to=0.97 r=0.077 r2=0.082 deep=0.78 blend=0.0050 mirror color=d9d8d9 gloss=0.10
  blob leg on shin  at=1.00 r=0.085 deep=0.78 blend=0.0050 mirror color=d9d8d9 gloss=0.10

  # ============================================================
  # SHOES — dark near-black brown 201109, flat mary-jane toes, sole grey
  # bdb9bc. Mesh sole band: 0.292 wide (shoe half-width 0.073 either side of
  # centres at x +/-0.073), collar 0.299 at the ankle. Two prims a side,
  # authored as world displacements off the foot bone (head = the ankle).
  # ============================================================
  # Body: heel (0.073, 0.030, -0.045) to toe, yawed OUT ~8 deg (the mesh's
  # toes-out stance shows in its sole footprint being nearly SQUARE —
  # 0.292 wide x 0.289 deep) — toe at (0.091, 0.031, 0.058), wide 2.4 ->
  # 0.072/0.062 half-width, z -0.077..0.085 (mesh side depth 0.152-0.170).
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.030 r2=0.026 wide=2.40 tall=1.05 deep=1.05 blend=0.0060 offset=(0.004,-0.089,-0.045) tip=(0.018,0.001,0.103) mirror color=201109 gloss=0.20
  # Vamp/collar wrapping the ankle: the mesh's 0.114-0.147 bands run
  # 0.304-0.318 wide — 0.090 half-width at x 0.073 (wide 1.88).
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.048 wide=1.88 tall=0.95 deep=1.55 blend=0.0060 offset=(0.004,-0.040,0.012) mirror color=201109 gloss=0.20
  # THE SOLE (v3): a thin capsule tracing the shoe's OWN yawed footprint,
  # inset under the upper. v2's plate (wide 2.30 x deep 4.00 = 0.15 x 0.26
  # at floor level, four times the shoe's depth, light bdb9bc) read as a
  # white OVAL she stood on (owner, 2026-08-23) — but the mesh's sole is a
  # thin grey EDGE, not a platform: its side bands run 0.258-0.289 at the
  # sole because of the toes-out splay, and the shoe body above is only
  # 0.152-0.170 deep. So: same heel->toe run and 8-deg yaw as the upper
  # (offset/tip copied from the shoe body line above), radii a hair inside
  # it (wide 2.10 vs 2.40, deep 0.95 vs 1.05) so no rim shows past the shoe
  # from the front or the side, and darkened bdb9bc -> 655c5e toward the
  # shoe's 201109. The bottom stays at y~0: axis at -0.110 with half-height
  # 0.18*r puts the tread where v2's plate bottom was (the 1.70 m height
  # pin marches y 0.002 for flesh).
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.030 r2=0.026 wide=2.10 tall=0.18 deep=0.95 blend=0.0040 offset=(0.004,-0.111,-0.045) tip=(0.018,0.001,0.103) mirror color=655c5e gloss=0.15

# ============================================================
# FACE BLOCK — the skin skull under the hair. Cranium 0.071 half-wide x
# 0.082 half-tall x 0.089 half-deep (mesh skin head ~0.143 wide under the
# 0.194 bob), centre 1.575. The jaw carries the chin: 0.041 half-wide
# (mesh chin 0.048 full-ish), bottom at 1.4535 via jawDrop 0.075. Features
# deliberately SUBTLE — the eyes and mouth are painted prims above.
# ============================================================
face
  # 0.078 (was 0.075) and taller below: the face read vertically squeezed
  # against the mesh's tall open oval once the fringe retreated.
  headRadius 0.078
  headWidth  0.95
  # 1.22 (was 1.10): the cranium's bottom must reach toward the mouth
  # latitude — the mesh has 0.07-wide cheeks at y 1.50 where a shorter
  # cranium has already tapered to a point.
  headHeight 1.30
  headDepth  1.19
  # 0.95 (was 0.70): the mesh's lower face is 0.146 wide at mouth height
  # (its muzzle plan), not the 0.08 the chin row alone suggested.
  jawWidth   0.95
  jawHeight  0.80
  jawDrop    0.075
  # The chin juts: the mesh's front profile runs 0.101-0.123 at 1.44-1.48.
  jawJut     0.045
  # A small button nose — 2 mm. Tanida faces have almost no nose mass; more
  # would break the clean profile the head check wants (+-0.03 crown to chin).
  noseLength 0.002
  noseWidth  0.30
  noseDrop   0.028
  browHeavy  0.003
  browRise   0.026
  headBlend  0.0045

# The sheet is a DECAL: `npm run blob:face-bake -- schoolgirl` renders the
# mesh head orthographically from the front into a 512 square, head box
# 0.216 wide x 0.280 tall centred at y 1.56 (the script prints these). The
# projection maps skull space (hs = offset / the fattest head prim's
# semi-axes — here the crown shell, centre y 1.612, half 0.098 x 0.082) to
# image uv: uv = hs * scale + centre, uv.y from the BOTTOM of the image.
# scaleX = 0.098/0.280 = 0.35 keeps the mesh's proportions sideways. The
# vertical is NOT the literal 0.29/0.69 that proportion gives: aim the two
# features. With the head-rework face (fringe raised to ~1.556, taller
# cranium), the image's eyes (uv.y 0.40 from the bottom) sit at 1.52 and
# the mouth (0.17) at 1.478 — hs -1.09 and -1.60 — giving scaleY 0.45,
# centreY 0.89. scaleX 0.38, a touch over the proportional 0.35, keeps the
# eyes off the cheek curve where the planar projection starts to bend.
# History: literal 0.29/0.69 put the eyes against the fringe and the mouth
# under the chin; 0.42/0.90 and 0.54/1.00 each lost part of the mouth under
# the pre-rework jaw (shots 2026-08-23).
# The agents' painted faces never read (v1 and v2 both); the mesh's own
# face, flat, does — old PSX faces were painted on too.
sheet
  image       schoolgirl-face.png
  decal       1
  projScaleX  0.38
  projScaleY  0.45
  projCentreX 0.5
  projCentreY 0.89

# Skin dab18a = sRGB (218,177,138) -> linear (0.699, 0.439, 0.254). Wounds
# stay red. Toy-clean: no mottle to speak of, no surface or silhouette
# noise, moderate gloss (specRoughness 0.35 per the style brief).
palette
  baseColor     0.699 0.439 0.254
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.08
  charColor     0.22 0.13 0.10
  specIntensity 0.45
  specRoughness 0.35
  fresnelBoost  0.30
  translucency  0.22
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.0
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.0
  wetness       0.12
  mottleAmp     0.02
  mottleScale   1.2
  mottleColor   0.55 0.38 0.22
